{"kind":"stack","id":"s-env-change","title":"Environments can change: dangers to living things","theme":{"background":"#F4F9F1","foreground":"#1F3B24","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"A forest fire burns down many trees. What is one danger this poses to the animals that lived there?"},{"type":"image","picto":"fire"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a1","label":"They lose their homes and food","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a2","label":"They grow bigger and stronger","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a3","label":"They learn to fly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Habitat"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"The natural place where a plant or animal lives and finds food, water and shelter."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"A river becomes polluted with oil. Why is this dangerous for fish?"},{"type":"image","picto":"fish"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a1","label":"The oil blocks the oxygen they need to breathe in the water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a2","label":"The oil makes the water warmer and sweeter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a3","label":"The oil gives them extra energy to swim faster","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which change in an environment is most likely to be caused by people?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a1","label":"Cutting down a forest to build houses","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a2","label":"The leaves changing colour in autumn","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a3","label":"Snow falling in winter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"A heavy storm floods the field where a family of hedgehogs lives. What should the hedgehogs do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a1","label":"Move to higher ground under the hedge","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a2","label":"Stay in the nest and wait","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The hedgehogs climb to dry ground and stay safe until the water goes down."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The water rises into the nest and the hedgehogs get cold and wet."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"How many quiz questions did you answer in this stack?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a1","label":"Five","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a2","label":"Three","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a3","label":"Seven","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Pollution"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"Harmful substances added to air, water or soil that can damage living things."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a good way to protect a habitat from pollution?"},{"type":"image","picto":"tree"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a1","label":"Picking up litter and recycling rubbish","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a2","label":"Throwing rubbish into the river","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a3","label":"Burning rubbish in the woods","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you explored how environments change"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Changes in our environment can be dangerous for living things. Keep looking for ways to protect the places where plants and animals live."}],"actions":[]}}
